{
 "what": "What git was handed when a command hands a string to another shell (FN-55), command by command. `argv` is every git started from outside git, in order, with its whole argv as git itself wrote it down (the trace2 start event, GIT_TRACE2_EVENT); an empty list: no git ran.",
 "how": "A `posix` case was written to a file and run as a script by Git Bash; a `powershell` case was run as a script block by PowerShell 7. Each in a scratch repository with no hooks and nothing staged, so nothing was committed.",
